{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>In the house, horror</b> — the meaning: a repulsive thing, like figs that are pressed together [and spoil]." "<b>There is harlotry for Ephraim</b> — an allusion to the calves in Bethel, which belongs to Ephraim."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra reads שערורית via its rare biblical sense of something repulsive; the fig analogy is hyper-literal and the comparison remains cryptic."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:50:25.251283210Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}